/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless

# Java ME runs in its own tab: CheerpJ embeds a frame from its CDN that cannot
# satisfy cross-origin isolation, so these pages drop it (nothing here needs
# SharedArrayBuffer).
/j2me/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  ! Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy

# —— iOS: the emulator frames ask for require-corp ————————————————————————
#
# Safari has never supported COEP: credentialless — it only accepts require-corp
# — so on iPhone and iPad none of this site is cross-origin isolated, which
# means no SharedArrayBuffer, which means no threads in any emulator. That is
# the single biggest reason the console is worse on Apple hardware.
#
# The main document cannot switch: require-corp blocks every cross-origin
# no-cors subresource, and that document embeds YouTube, Spotify, map tiles and
# remote thumbnails. (CORS-mode fetch() is unaffected either way — COEP does not
# police it — so none of the site's ~19 JSON APIs are at stake here.)
#
# But COEP is per document, and the heavy emulators each run in their own
# same-origin frame that loads nothing cross-origin at all. Those frames can ask
# for the stricter policy without the main document changing, which is what
# gives Safari its threads. Audited: every path below has no cross-origin
# subresource of any kind.
#
# Not listed, deliberately:
#   · EmulatorJS mounts in the TOP document (iframes lose gamepad access — see
#     emulator/GameSession.tsx), so it shares the main document's policy and
#     cannot be isolated without taking YouTube and the rest down with it.
#   · jazz2 loads googletagmanager, micropolis loads snap.berkeley.edu.

# Only the directories that no Pages Function serves. quake, duke, diablo,
# openttd, descent, gorescript, hexgl and openhv are handed to
# functions/<dir>/[[file]].ts, and a Function's response never passes through
# _headers — those set the same policy in r2serve.ts instead. Both lists were
# audited the same way and have to stay in step.

/play/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/play/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/play-mt/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/play-mt/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/play-tune/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/play-tune/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/wolf/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/wolf/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/jazz/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/jazz/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Self-hosted builds that are not in this repository (see src/webgames.ts).
# Both want threads — Source is a threaded engine, and a recompilation expects
# the same — and both are same-origin-only, so they take the strict policy too.
# Harmless when absent: a rule for a path that 404s changes nothing.
/hl2/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/hl2/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/pepsiman/*
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/pepsiman/
  ! Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
